Manufacturing Yield and Qualification Remain Key Challenges

Producing high-quality vias through glass requires precise processing and control of via geometry, surface quality and metallization. Defects, cracks, thermal mismatch and process variation can affect package reliability.

Manufacturers must also establish compatibility with wafer handling, assembly and inspection processes. Scaling from pilot manufacturing to high-volume production requires repeatable yield and validated downstream performance.

